WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.200
Every president attempts to frame his
first national security strategy as a

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:12.900
break from his predecessors. President
Trump is no different.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.580
But what's striking is how traditional
the goals of the new strategy are:

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:21.779
protect the homeland; promote American
prosperity; preserve peace through

00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:27.060
military strength; and advance American
influence through diplomacy, alliances,

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:32.099
help for fragile states, and by
advocating for American values. Add in

00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:35.700
the strategy's larger goal of ensuring
a favorable balance of power in Asia,

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.680
Europe, and the Middle East – a goal that
has been the cornerstone of American

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.210
grand strategy for decades – and it's hard
to say that this strategy's broader

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:50.520
sweep is especially new. Ironically, if
there is a break from the past, it's with

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.899
candidate Trump's statements on foreign
policy, statements that were often more

00:00:54.899 --> 00:00:58.890
isolationist, more protectionist, and
typically harsher towards allies than

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:03.270
adversaries like Russia. For those of us
who think that the traditional strategy

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:06.260
has served the U.S. well, this is all to the good.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:13.220
Do you think President Trump will commit to his new strategy, or will he revert to policies he outlined in his

00:01:13.229 --> 00:01:18.509
campaign? Let us know in your comments.
Also, let us know what other topics you'd

00:01:18.509 --> 00:01:23.759
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,
and be sure to like and subscribe for

00:01:23.759 --> 00:01:28.159
more research and videos from AEI.

